  "title": "Why Moving Employment Verification Earlier in the Hiring Cycle Reduces Bad Hires",
  "summary": "Most companies verify employment after the offer — after interviews, reference calls, and negotiation are already spent on unverified resumes. Move it to right after the phone screen and verification becomes an early filter, not a final gate, so a disqualifying finding costs one phone screen, not the whole funnel.",
